--- a/serve_realtime_ws.py
+++ b/serve_realtime_ws.py

 Adds SEGMENT_END WebSocket command to the FunASR streaming server.

 When the client's local VAD detects end-of-speech, it sends "SEGMENT_END"
 (text message). The server force-decodes the current audio segment, locks it
 as a sentence, resets VAD state, and continues accepting audio on the same
 connection. This avoids reconnection overhead while using the client's
 superior VAD for sentence boundary detection.

 Protocol:
   START → binary audio... → SEGMENT_END → (sentence returned) → binary audio... → STOP

 Changes:
 1. RealtimeASRSession.force_segment_end() method
 2. handle_client: SEGMENT_END command handler (responds with event="segment_end")
